```java
// Statement — static SQL only (no input)
try (Statement st = con.createStatement();
     ResultSet rs = st.executeQuery("SELECT COUNT(*) FROM users")) { /* ... */ }

// PreparedStatement — parameterized, safe (the default)
try (PreparedStatement ps = con.prepareStatement("SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?")) {
    ps.setInt(1, 42);
    try (ResultSet rs = ps.executeQuery()) { /* ... */ }
}

// CallableStatement — stored procedure
try (CallableStatement cs = con.prepareCall("{call get_user(?)}")) {
    cs.setInt(1, 42);
    cs.execute();
}
```

```java
// NEVER do this — input is part of the SQL
String name = request.getParameter("name");   // attacker: ' OR '1'='1
String sql = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE name = '" + name + "'";
Statement st = con.createStatement();
ResultSet rs = st.executeQuery(sql);
// becomes: SELECT * FROM users WHERE name = '' OR '1'='1'  -> returns everyone
```

```java
String name = request.getParameter("name");
try (PreparedStatement ps =
        con.prepareStatement("SELECT * FROM users WHERE name = ?")) {
    ps.setString(1, name);   // bound as DATA, never as SQL
    try (ResultSet rs = ps.executeQuery()) { /* ... */ }
}
// even ' OR '1'='1 is treated as a literal name string -> no injection
```

*The query is parsed before the value is bound, so input can't alter its structure.*

